[FEN "r1b1kbnr/1pp2ppp/p1p5/4N3/3qP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 6"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1b1kbnr/1pp2ppp/p1p5/4N3/3qP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R_w_KQkq_-_1_6"]

{ The same Spanish trap: your queen in the middle hits his knight and the pawn behind it. Watch his reply. }
6. Nxf7 { His knight grabs the pawn beside your king and attacks your rook. Greedy, because pulling the knight back was his move. What now? } 6... Qxe4+ { Check first! Your queen takes his king pawn, and he must answer the check before he can save his knight. [%cal Ge4e1] } (6... Kxf7 { You win his knight at once, but you leave him his king pawn. } 7. d3 { He guards his king pawn, so you won a knight for two pawns instead of for one. }) 7. Qe2 { He blocks the check with his queen, and now she attacks yours. What now? } 7... Qxe2+ { Your queen takes his with check, so his king must take back before his knight can run. } (7... Kxf7 { You take the knight, but his queen is still attacking yours. } 8. Qxe4 { His queen takes yours, and the game is lost. }) 8. Kxe2 { His king takes back, and his knight is still sitting right next to your king. } 8... Kxf7 { Your king takes the knight. You won a knight for a pawn, because you checked before you took. [%csl Gf7] } (8... Bg4+ { A check, but this one only helps him: his pawn blocks it and then takes your bishop. } 9. f3 Kxf7 10. fxg4 { You won the knight, but his pawn took your bishop, so the extra piece is gone. }) 0-1
